Creating a character requires generating the basic abilities of your
adventurer, understanding their cultural and upbringings, choosing a
class, defining their allies, and preparing for adventure.

During character creation you may accrue blessings of Chaos for
embracing serendipity, keep track of the total number of these. At the
end of character creation each will influence their life in interesting
ways.

+ Roll characteristics
+ Culture
+ Background
+ Class
+ Class kit
+ Starting gear
+ Hit points
+ Name, backstory

=== Roll Characteristics
<roll-characteristics>
Characters have six \[\[Game Rules/Characteristics|Characteristics\]\]:
Strength, Dexterity, Constitution, Wisdom, Intelligence, and Charisma -
usually between 3 and 18.

- Strength: melee attack and damage rolls, carrying capacity
- Dexterity: armor class ranged weapons, reflex saves
- Constitution: hit points, saves against poison and physical effects
- Intelligence: spell points, bonus skill points
- Wisdom: saves against mental and magical effects, avoiding surprise
  and ambush, teaching
- Charisma: reaction rolls, Leadership score

Roll a set of 3d6 four times in a row and write down these numbers. From
here you have a choice: - Roll two more sets of 3d6, assign each of
these six numbers to your six characteristics, gain 2 blessings of Chaos
\- Ignore the prior rolls and use a static array. Assign 15, 12, 10, 10,
9, 7 to your characteristics.

For each characteristic write down its corresponding modifier.

