==== Beast Kingdoms
<beast-kingdoms>
- Languages: Noctian, Psuedophidian
- 2 skill points in Beastmastery, Heal, Seneschal, Alteration
- Head of a heraldic animal, as the \[\[Game Rules/Classes and Character
  Creation/Expertise/Traits/Animal Aspect|Animal Aspect\]\] trait, based
  on your background
- Born in 1d4: 1 - the domain of grand Chimericon under Prince Cyrus
  `<x, y, z>`

These kingdoms are a contentious group of fiefdoms held together by a
rigid caste system, where people have the heads of animals. Long ago the
people of the Beast Kingdoms lived deep within Noctis Labyrinthus, until
the coming of ash and the death of the Fates drove them out. What
remains in Noctis are only strange and twisted beasts.

The princes hold near absolute power within their domains, and life is
harshly dictated by numerous taboos; forbidden the eating of certain
foods, forbidding the use of many colors of dress by the lower classes,
and circumscribing life on all fronts.

Covered more in \[\[Game Rules/Classes and Character Creation/Cultural
Background/Secrets of the Beast Kingdoms|Secrets of the Beast
Kingdoms\]\].

==== Alcheran
<alcheran>
- Languages: Alcheran, Psuedophidian
- 2 skill points in Athletics, Artisanry, Diplomacy, Trade
- Gain 6 points in Background skills instead of the normal 5
- Born in 1d4: 1 - the vast halls of Labyrinth, 2 - the hinterlands
  beyond Labyrinth, 3 - the former glory of the City of Glass, 4 - a
  smaller city state who's nature you help determine with your GM

Alcherans pride themselves on the democratic lineage of their
city-states, where citizenship is granted to those who excel at a city's
chosen form of artisanry. Within Labyrinth the creation of books is of
uptmost importance, as exemplified by the grand temple to Heron atop the
acropolis.

